Subject: «About» — the version of the vendored interface, not of the application

A porting fix, not a feature.

Upstream's `Qt.application.version` is the version of ITS application, i.e.
of the waywallen interface. Here the page is shown by another application
with its own version (and `Qt.application.version` is empty there, so the
line read as «Версия»). We take the version of the vendored interface — the
tag `ui/UPSTREAM_TAG`, which Rexon exposes as `W.App.uiVersion`
(`rust/rexon-gui/src/we_app.rs`, the tag is parsed by
`rexon_core::qml_modules::ui_version`); the application-wide property is not
replaced.

v0.5.0: upstream added a second line «Daemon version %1» — visible when the
daemon version differs from `Qt.application.version`. The previous form of
the patch (line 1 = daemon version) would have shown the version twice, so
both references to `Qt.application.version` are replaced with one property:
line 1 — the interface, line 2 — the daemon when they differ (a real case
for Rexon: the system daemon is older or newer than the embedded QML).

Logo: since 19.10.2026 Rexon puts it into its own resources at the upstream
address (`rust/rexon-gui/waywallen_assets.qrc`), no markup edit is needed for
it. The patch file name is kept as before.
---
diff --git a/ui/qml/page/AboutPage.qml b/ui/qml/page/AboutPage.qml
index 2a01c6f..adbc7be 100644
--- a/ui/qml/page/AboutPage.qml
+++ b/ui/qml/page/AboutPage.qml
@@ -44,7 +44,15 @@ MD.Page {
 
         MD.Text {
             Layout.alignment: Qt.AlignHCenter
-            text: qsTr("Version %1").arg(Qt.application.version)
+            // REXON EDIT (a porting fix, not a feature): upstream has
+            // `Qt.application.version` here — the APPLICATION version, i.e. of its
+            // interface. Inside Rexon the page is shown by another application
+            // with its own version (`Qt.application.version` is empty for us), so
+            // we take the version of the VENDORED interface — the tag from `ui/UPSTREAM_TAG`,
+            // which Rexon exposes as `W.App.uiVersion`. The meaning is the same
+            // as upstream: line 1 — the interface, line 2 — the daemon, if
+            // its version differs.
+            text: qsTr("Version %1").arg(W.App.uiVersion)
             typescale: MD.Token.typescale.body_medium
             color: MD.Token.color.on_surface_variant
         }
@@ -54,7 +62,7 @@ MD.Page {
 
             Layout.alignment: Qt.AlignHCenter
             Layout.topMargin: -12
-            visible: daemonVersion.length > 0 && daemonVersion !== Qt.application.version
+            visible: daemonVersion.length > 0 && daemonVersion !== W.App.uiVersion
             text: qsTr("Daemon version %1").arg(daemonVersion)
             typescale: MD.Token.typescale.body_medium
             color: MD.Token.color.on_surface_variant
